# Git workflow

- After creating any commit, ALWAYS push to `main` automatically (`git push origin HEAD:main`). Do not ask the user for permission to push.
- Still only *create* commits when the user asks for one (the auto-push rule applies to commits the user requested).
- This shell is PowerShell: do NOT use `&&`, `||`, or heredocs (`<<'EOF'`). Chain commands with `;`, and pass multi-line commit messages via `git commit -F <file>`.
